IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`
IMPORT `ssc3-a-s43-s44`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, ss 44A, 44B and 44C (part ssc3).
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- Deemed earnings factors (ss 44A, 44B) and earnings factor credits (s 44C), for the pensioner's earnings
-- factor under s 44(6)(za). "The first appointed year" and "the flat rate introduction year" are defined
-- outside this range (s 122 and the Pensions Act 2014 provisions the Act borrows); whether a year is one of
-- them is a fact the person states.
-- "Throughout the year" and "any part of that week" are facts the person states.

§ `Part II: deemed earnings factors and credits`

§§ `Section 44A: deemed earnings factors`

-- (A1): subsections (1) to (4) apply to the first appointed year or any subsequent tax year before 2010-11.
-- src:1284 | (A1) Subsections (1) to (4) below apply to the first appointed year or any subsequent tax year before 2010-11.
@ref s 44A(A1) (src:1284)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
      `the year is the first appointed year or a later year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44A(A1) subsections (1) to (4) apply to the year` MEANS
    IF `the year is the first appointed year or a later year` AND year's `calendar year in which it begins` LESS THAN 2010
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says to which years (1) to (4) apply, not that they apply to no other

-- (2)(a): the pensioner would, apart from this section, have an earnings factor for the year equal to or greater
-- than the qualifying earnings factor but less than the low earnings threshold.
-- src:1289 | (a) the pensioner would, apart from this section, have an earnings factor for the year—
-- src:1290 | (i) equal to or greater than the qualifying earnings factor for the year; but
-- src:1291 | (ii) less than the low earnings threshold for the year;
@ref s 44A(2)(a) (src:1289-1291)
GIVEN `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the low earnings threshold for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44A(2)(a) the earnings factor lies from the qualifying earnings factor up to the low earnings threshold` MEANS
        `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section` AT LEAST `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
    AND `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section` LESS THAN `the low earnings threshold for the year`

-- (2)(b): carer's allowance was payable throughout the year, or would have been but for a reduction to nil
-- under regulations because of other benefits.
-- src:1292 | (b) carer’s allowance—
-- src:1293 | (i) was payable to the pensioner throughout the year; or
-- src:1294 | (ii) would have been so payable but for the fact that under regulations the amount payable to him was reduced to nil because of his receipt of other benefits;
@ref s 44A(2)(b) (src:1292-1294)
GIVEN `carer's allowance was payable to the pensioner throughout the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `carer's allowance would have been so payable but for a reduction to nil under regulations because of the pensioner's receipt of other benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44A(2)(b) carer's allowance condition` MEANS
    `carer's allowance was payable to the pensioner throughout the year`
    OR `carer's allowance would have been so payable but for a reduction to nil under regulations because of the pensioner's receipt of other benefits`

-- (2)(c): the pensioner is taken, for paragraph 5(7)(b) of Schedule 3, to be precluded from regular employment by
-- responsibilities at home throughout the year by virtue of (i) child benefit payable in respect of a child
-- under the age of six, or (ii) satisfying another prescribed condition.
-- "under the age of six" is s 173's answer (seam K2).
-- src:1295 | (c) for the purposes of paragraph 5(7)(b) of Schedule 3, the pensioner is taken to be precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home throughout the year by virtue of—
-- src:1296 | (i) the fact that child benefit was payable to him in respect of a child under the age of six; or
-- src:1297 | (ii) his satisfying such other condition as may be prescribed;
@ref s 44A(2)(c) (src:1295-1297)
GIVEN `child benefit was payable to the pensioner throughout the year in respect of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the child is under 6` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner satisfies another condition prescribed for the purposes of paragraph (c)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44A(2)(c) responsibilities at home condition` MEANS
    `ssc3 helper any of`
        (LIST
            `ssc3 helper all of` (LIST JUST `child benefit was payable to the pensioner throughout the year in respect of a child`, `s 173(a) the child is under 6`)
          , JUST `the pensioner satisfies another condition prescribed for the purposes of paragraph (c)(ii)`)

-- (2)(d): the pensioner satisfies the requirement in subsection (3) and long-term incapacity benefit or qualifying
-- employment and support allowance was payable throughout the year, or would have been but for (i) failing the
-- contribution conditions or (ii) a reduction to nil because of other benefits or payments from an occupational or
-- personal pension scheme (meanings: subsection (6), seam S13).
-- src:1298 | (d) the pensioner is a person satisfying the requirement in subsection (3) below to whom long-term incapacity benefit or qualifying employment and support allowance was payable throughout the year, or would have been so payable but for the fact that—
-- src:1299 | (i) he did not satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 or, as the case may be, in paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 1 to the Welfare Reform Act 2007; or
-- src:1300 | (ii) under regulations the amount payable to him was reduced to nil because of his receipt of other benefits or of payments from an occupational pension scheme or personal pension scheme.
@ref s 44A(2)(d) (src:1298-1300)
GIVEN `the pensioner satisfies the requirement in subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `long-term incapacity benefit or qualifying employment and support allowance was payable to the pensioner throughout the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner did not satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 or paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 1 to the Welfare Reform Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under regulations the amount payable was reduced to nil because of the pensioner's receipt of other benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under regulations the amount payable was reduced to nil because of the pensioner's receipt of payments from a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 30DD(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30DD(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44A(2)(d) incapacity benefit condition` MEANS
    `ssc3 helper all of`
        (LIST
            `the pensioner satisfies the requirement in subsection (3)`
          , `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    JUST `long-term incapacity benefit or qualifying employment and support allowance was payable to the pensioner throughout the year`
                  , JUST `the pensioner did not satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 or paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 1 to the Welfare Reform Act 2007`
                  , JUST `under regulations the amount payable was reduced to nil because of the pensioner's receipt of other benefits`
                  , `ssc3 helper all of`
                        (LIST
                            JUST `under regulations the amount payable was reduced to nil because of the pensioner's receipt of payments from a scheme`
                          , `ssc3 helper any of` (LIST `s 30DD(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme`, `s 30DD(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme`))))

-- (2) together with (1): "if any of the conditions in subsection (2) below is satisfied".
-- src:1285 | (1) For the purposes of section 44(6)(za) above, if any of the conditions in subsection (2) below is satisfied for a relevant year to which this subsection applies, a pensioner is deemed to have an earnings factor for that year which—
-- src:1286 | (a) is derived from so much of his earnings as did not exceed the applicable limit and on which primary Class 1 contributions were paid; and
-- src:1287 | (b) is equal to the amount which, when added to any other earnings factors taken into account under that provision, produces an aggregate of earnings factors equal to the low earnings threshold.
-- src:1288 | (2) The conditions referred to in subsection (1) above are that—
@ref s 44A(1) and (2), the conditions (src:1285-1288)
GIVEN `condition (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `condition (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44A(2) any of the conditions in subsection (2) is satisfied` MEANS
    `ssc3 helper any of` (LIST JUST `condition (a)`, JUST `condition (b)`, `condition (c)`, `condition (d)`)

-- (1): the deemed earnings factor is the amount that, added to any other earnings factors taken into account under
-- s 44(6), gives an aggregate equal to the low earnings threshold. Where no condition is satisfied the subsection
-- deems nothing.  Where the other factors already exceed the threshold the text names no amount.
-- src:1285 | (1) For the purposes of section 44(6)(za) above, if any of the conditions in subsection (2) below is satisfied for a relevant year to which this subsection applies, a pensioner is deemed to have an earnings factor for that year which—
-- src:1286 | (a) is derived from so much of his earnings as did not exceed the applicable limit and on which primary Class 1 contributions were paid; and
-- src:1287 | (b) is equal to the amount which, when added to any other earnings factors taken into account under that provision, produces an aggregate of earnings factors equal to the low earnings threshold.
@ref s 44A(1) (src:1285-1287)
GIVEN `any of the conditions in subsection (2) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the low earnings threshold for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the other earnings factors taken into account under section 44(6)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 44A(1) the deemed earnings factor in pounds` MEANS
    IF `any of the conditions in subsection (2) is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the other earnings factors taken into account under section 44(6)` AT MOST `the low earnings threshold for the year`
    THEN JUST (`the low earnings threshold for the year` MINUS `the other earnings factors taken into account under section 44(6)`)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the pensioner is deemed to have a factor "if any of the conditions ... is satisfied"; no amount is named where the other factors already exceed the threshold

-- (4)(a): a pensioner's working life does not include (i) a tax year before 1978-79 or (ii) a year in which he is
-- deemed under (1) to have a factor by virtue of (2)(b) or (c).
-- src:1304 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3)(b) above—
-- src:1305 | (a) a pensioner’s working life shall not include—
-- src:1306 | (i) any tax year before 1978-79; or
-- src:1307 | (ii) any year in which he is deemed under subsection (1) above to have an earnings factor by virtue of fulfilling the condition in subsection (2)(b) or (c) above; and
@ref s 44A(4)(a) (src:1304-1307)
GIVEN `the number of tax years in the pensioner's working life before the exclusions` IS A NUMBER
      `of which the number before 1978-79` IS A NUMBER
      `of which the number in which the pensioner is deemed under subsection (1) to have a factor by virtue of subsection (2)(b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 44A(4)(a) the pensioner's working life in years` MEANS
    `the number of tax years in the pensioner's working life before the exclusions`
    MINUS `of which the number before 1978-79`
    MINUS `of which the number in which the pensioner is deemed under subsection (1) to have a factor by virtue of subsection (2)(b) or (c)`

-- (4)(b): the working life divided by ten, rounded to the nearest whole year, a half year rounded down.
-- src:1304 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3)(b) above—
-- src:1305 | (a) a pensioner’s working life shall not include—
-- src:1306 | (i) any tax year before 1978-79; or
-- src:1307 | (ii) any year in which he is deemed under subsection (1) above to have an earnings factor by virtue of fulfilling the condition in subsection (2)(b) or (c) above; and
-- src:1308 | (b) the figure calculated by dividing his working life by ten shall be rounded to the nearest whole year (and any half year shall be rounded down).
@ref s 44A(4)(b) (src:1304-1308)
GIVEN `the pensioner's working life in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 44A(4)(b) one tenth of the working life rounded to the nearest whole year` MEANS
    CEILING ((`the pensioner's working life in years` DIVIDED BY 10) MINUS 0.5)

-- (3): the requirement is that (a) for one or more relevant years the pensioner has paid, or is treated as having
-- paid, primary Class 1 contributions on earnings equal to or greater than the qualifying earnings factor, and
-- (b) the years for which he has such a factor are at least one tenth of his working life.
-- src:1301 | (3) The requirement referred to in subsection (2)(d) above is that—
-- src:1302 | (a) for one or more relevant years the pensioner has paid, or (apart from this section) is treated as having paid, primary Class 1 contributions on earnings equal to or greater than the qualifying earnings factor; and
-- src:1303 | (b) the years for which he has such a factor constitute at least one tenth of his working life.
@ref s 44A(3) (src:1301-1303)
GIVEN `the number of relevant years for which the pensioner has a factor equal to or greater than the qualifying earnings factor` IS A NUMBER
      `one tenth of the working life rounded to the nearest whole year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44A(3) the requirement referred to in subsection (2)(d) is satisfied` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirement referred to in subsection (2)(d) above is that" -- a definition, so a failed limb is the text's no
        `the number of relevant years for which the pensioner has a factor equal to or greater than the qualifying earnings factor` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the number of relevant years for which the pensioner has a factor equal to or greater than the qualifying earnings factor` AT LEAST `one tenth of the working life rounded to the nearest whole year`

-- (4A): the requirement in (2)(d) and subsections (3) and (4) "do not apply to a pensioner attaining pensionable
-- age on or after 6th April 2010".
-- src:1309 | (4A) The following do not apply to a pensioner attaining pensionable age on or after 6th April 2010—
-- src:1310 | (a) the requirement referred to in subsection (2)(d) above, and
-- src:1311 | (b) subsections (3) and (4) above.
@ref s 44A(4A) (src:1309-1311)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44A(4A) the requirement in subsection (2)(d) and subsections (3) and (4) apply to the pensioner` MEANS
    IF pensioner's `date of attaining pensionable age` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 2010)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following do not apply to a pensioner attaining pensionable age on or after 6th April 2010"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says to whom they do not apply, not to whom they do

-- (5): the low earnings threshold for the first appointed year and later tax years is 9,500 pounds, "but subject
-- to section 148A of the Administration Act": an alteration under that section is an input.
-- src:1312 | (5) The low earnings threshold for the first appointed year and subsequent tax years shall be £9,500 (but subject to section 148A of the Administration Act).
@ref s 44A(5) (src:1312)
GIVEN `the year is the first appointed year or a later year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the figure the threshold has been altered to under section 148A of the Administration Act` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 44A(5) the low earnings threshold in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the year is the first appointed year or a later year`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the figure the threshold has been altered to under section 148A of the Administration Act`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 9500
        WHEN JUST altered THEN JUST altered
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the threshold is stated "for the first appointed year and subsequent tax years"

-- (5A): "the applicable limit" in (1)(a) has the same meaning as in section 44.
-- src:1313 | (5A) In subsection (1)(a) “the applicable limit” has the same meaning as in section 44.
@ref s 44A(5A) (src:1313)
GIVEN limits IS A `Earnings limits`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 44A(5A) the applicable limit in pounds` MEANS `s 44(7)(c) the applicable limit in pounds` limits

-- (6): "occupational pension scheme" and "personal pension scheme" have the meanings given by s 30DD(6) (another
-- part's answers, seam S13).
-- src:1314 | (6) In subsection (2)(d)(ii) above, “occupational pension scheme” and “personal pension scheme” have the meanings given by subsection (6) of section 30DD above for the purposes of subsection (5) of that section.
@ref s 44A(6) (src:1314)
GIVEN `s 30DD(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44A(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` MEANS `s 30DD(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme`

-- src:1314 | (6) In subsection (2)(d)(ii) above, “occupational pension scheme” and “personal pension scheme” have the meanings given by subsection (6) of section 30DD above for the purposes of subsection (5) of that section.
@ref s 44A(6) (src:1314)
GIVEN `s 30DD(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44A(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme` MEANS `s 30DD(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme`

-- (7): "qualifying employment and support allowance" means contributory employment and support allowance where
-- (a) payable for a continuous period of 52 weeks; (b) it included the support component; or (c) for a man born
-- between 6 April 1944 and 5 April 1947, or a woman born between 6 April 1949 and 5 April 1951, payable for a
-- continuous period of 13 weeks immediately following a period throughout which statutory sick pay was payable.
-- src:1315 | (7) In subsection (2)(d) “qualifying employment and support allowance” means contributory employment and support allowance where—
-- src:1316 | (a) that allowance was payable for a continuous period of 52 weeks;
-- src:1317 | (b) that allowance included the support component under section 2(2) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007; or
-- src:1318 | (c) in the case of—
-- src:1319 | (i) a man born between 6th April 1944 and 5th April 1947; or
-- src:1320 | (ii) a woman born between 6th April 1949 and 5th April 1951,
-- src:1321 | that allowance was payable for a continuous period of 13 weeks immediately following a period throughout which statutory sick pay was payable.
@ref s 44A(7) (src:1315-1321)
GIVEN pensioner IS A Person
      `the allowance is contributory employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks for which the allowance was payable continuously` IS A NUMBER
      `the allowance included the support component under section 2(2) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allowance was payable for a continuous period of 13 weeks immediately following a period throughout which statutory sick pay was payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44A(7) the allowance is qualifying employment and support allowance` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"qualifying employment and support allowance\" means contributory employment and support allowance where"
        `the allowance is contributory employment and support allowance`
    AND (    `the number of weeks for which the allowance was payable continuously` AT LEAST 52
         OR `the allowance included the support component under section 2(2) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007`
         OR (    `the allowance was payable for a continuous period of 13 weeks immediately following a period throughout which statutory sick pay was payable`
             AND (   (    pensioner's `sex` EQUALS Man
                      AND pensioner's `date of birth` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 1944)
                      AND pensioner's `date of birth` AT MOST (Date 5 4 1947))
                  OR (    pensioner's `sex` EQUALS Woman
                      AND pensioner's `date of birth` AT LEAST (Date 6 4 1949)
                      AND pensioner's `date of birth` AT MOST (Date 5 4 1951)))))

§§ `Section 44B: deemed earnings factors, 2010-11 onwards`

-- (1): this section applies to 2010-11 and subsequent tax years.
-- src:1323 | (1) This section applies to 2010-11 and subsequent tax years.
@ref s 44B(1) (src:1323)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44B(1) this section applies to the year` MEANS
    IF year's `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 2010
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says to which years the section applies; section 44A(A1) covers the earlier ones

-- (3): Condition A: the pensioner would, apart from this section, have an earnings factor equal to or greater than
-- the qualifying earnings factor but less than the low earnings threshold.
-- src:1327 | (3) Condition A is that the pensioner would, apart from this section, have an earnings factor for the year—
-- src:1328 | (a) equal to or greater than the qualifying earnings factor (“the QEF”) for the year, but
-- src:1329 | (b) less than the low earnings threshold for the year.
@ref s 44B(3) (src:1327-1329)
GIVEN `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the low earnings threshold for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44B(3) Condition A is satisfied` MEANS
        `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section` AT LEAST `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
    AND `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section` LESS THAN `the low earnings threshold for the year`

-- (4): Condition B: apart from this section and section 44C the earnings factor is less than the QEF, and the
-- pensioner is entitled to credits under section 44C equal to the difference between the QEF and that factor.
-- src:1330 | (4) Condition B is that the pensioner—
-- src:1331 | (a) would, apart from this section and section 44C below, have an earnings factor for the year less than the QEF for the year, but
-- src:1332 | (b) is entitled to an aggregate amount of earnings factor credits for that year under section 44C below equal to the difference between the QEF for the year and the earnings factor mentioned in paragraph (a) above.
@ref s 44B(4) (src:1330-1332)
GIVEN `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section and section 44C` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate amount of earnings factor credits the pensioner is entitled to for the year under section 44C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44B(4) Condition B is satisfied` MEANS
        `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section and section 44C` LESS THAN `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
    AND `the aggregate amount of earnings factor credits the pensioner is entitled to for the year under section 44C`
        EQUALS (`the qualifying earnings factor for the year` MINUS `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section and section 44C`)

-- (5): Condition C: the pensioner is entitled to 52 earnings factor credits for the year under section 44C.
-- (Read as "52 or more": a year with a fifty-third week in which the pensioner is eligible is not a year with
-- fewer credits; fork F5 in NOTES.md.)
-- src:1333 | (5) Condition C is that the pensioner is entitled to 52 earnings factor credits for that year under section 44C below.
@ref s 44B(5) (src:1333)
GIVEN `the number of earnings factor credits the pensioner is entitled to for the year under section 44C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44B(5) Condition C is satisfied` MEANS
    `the number of earnings factor credits the pensioner is entitled to for the year under section 44C` AT LEAST 52

-- (2) and (6): the deemed earnings factor where any of Conditions A to C is satisfied.
-- Before the flat rate introduction year it is the amount that brings the aggregate up to the low earnings threshold.
-- From that year, Condition A is omitted and (2)(b) refers to an aggregate greater than the QEF but less than the
-- threshold: a range, not an amount, so the text names no amount (fork F4 in NOTES.md) and the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:1324 | (2) For the purposes of section 44(6)(za) above, if any of Conditions A to C in subsections (3) to (5) below is satisfied for a relevant year to which this section applies, a pensioner is deemed to have an earnings factor for that year which—
-- src:1325 | (a) is derived from so much of his earnings as did not exceed the upper accrual point and on which primary Class 1 contributions were paid; and
-- src:1326 | (b) is equal to the amount which, when added to any other earnings factors taken into account under that provision, produces an aggregate of earnings factors equal to the low earnings threshold.
@ref s 44B(2) (src:1324-1326)
GIVEN `Condition A is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Condition B is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Condition C is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year is the flat rate introduction year or a later year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the low earnings threshold for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the other earnings factors taken into account under section 44(6)(za)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 44B(2) the deemed earnings factor in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the year is the flat rate introduction year or a later year` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 44B(6)(a) replaces "equal to" by "greater than the QEF, but less than the low earnings threshold", which names a range and no amount
        IF (`Condition A is satisfied` OR `Condition B is satisfied` OR `Condition C is satisfied`)
           AND `the other earnings factors taken into account under section 44(6)(za)` AT MOST `the low earnings threshold for the year`
        THEN JUST (`the low earnings threshold for the year` MINUS `the other earnings factors taken into account under section 44(6)(za)`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the pensioner is deemed to have the factor "if any of Conditions A to C ... is satisfied"

-- (6): from the flat rate introduction year, Condition A (and the reference to it in (2)) is omitted.
-- src:1334 | (6) This section has effect in relation to the flat rate introduction year and any subsequent tax year as if—
-- src:1335 | (a) subsection (2)(b) referred to an aggregate of earnings factors greater than the QEF, but less than the low earnings threshold, for the year (rather than to one equal to that threshold); and
-- src:1336 | (b) Condition A in subsection (3) (and the reference to it in subsection (2)) were omitted.
@ref s 44B(6) (src:1334-1336)
GIVEN `the year is the flat rate introduction year or a later year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44B(6)(b) Condition A is available` MEANS
    IF `the year is the flat rate introduction year or a later year`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition A in subsection (3) (and the reference to it in subsection (2)) were omitted"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph removes Condition A from later years and says nothing of the earlier ones

-- (6)(a): from the flat rate introduction year, an aggregate that (2)(b) refers to is one greater than the QEF
-- but less than the low earnings threshold; before it, one equal to the threshold.
-- src:1334 | (6) This section has effect in relation to the flat rate introduction year and any subsequent tax year as if—
-- src:1335 | (a) subsection (2)(b) referred to an aggregate of earnings factors greater than the QEF, but less than the low earnings threshold, for the year (rather than to one equal to that threshold); and
-- src:1336 | (b) Condition A in subsection (3) (and the reference to it in subsection (2)) were omitted.
@ref s 44B(6)(a) (src:1334-1336)
GIVEN `the year is the flat rate introduction year or a later year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate of earnings factors` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the low earnings threshold for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44B(6)(a) the aggregate is one that subsection (2)(b) refers to` MEANS
    IF `the year is the flat rate introduction year or a later year`
    THEN `the aggregate of earnings factors` GREATER THAN `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` AND `the aggregate of earnings factors` LESS THAN `the low earnings threshold for the year`
    ELSE `the aggregate of earnings factors` EQUALS `the low earnings threshold for the year`

-- (7)(b): "the low earnings threshold" is the threshold for the year concerned as specified in section 44A.
-- src:1339 | (b) “the low earnings threshold” means the low earnings threshold for the year concerned as specified in section 44A above; and
@ref s 44B(7)(b) (src:1339)
GIVEN `the year is the first appointed year or a later year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the figure the threshold has been altered to under section 148A of the Administration Act` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 44B(7)(b) the low earnings threshold in pounds` MEANS `s 44A(5) the low earnings threshold in pounds` `the year is the first appointed year or a later year` `the figure the threshold has been altered to under section 148A of the Administration Act`

-- (7)(c): in subsections (3) and (4), the pensioner's earnings factor for a relevant year is construed in accordance
-- with section 44(6)(za): the first appointed year or later, the factors from earnings up to the applicable limit.
-- src:1340 | (c) in subsections (3) and (4), any reference to the pensioner's earnings factor for a relevant year is to be construed in accordance with section 44(6)(za) above.
@ref s 44B(7)(c) (src:1340)
GIVEN `earnings factors derived from earnings up to the applicable limit on which primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 44B(7)(c) the pensioner's earnings factor for a relevant year` MEANS `earnings factors derived from earnings up to the applicable limit on which primary Class 1 contributions were paid or treated as paid`

§§ `Section 44C: earnings factor credits`

-- (1): this section applies, for Conditions B and C in section 44B(4) and (5), to 2010-11 and later tax years.
-- src:1342 | (1) This section applies, for the purposes of Conditions B and C in section 44B(4) and (5) above, to 2010-11 and subsequent tax years.
@ref s 44C(1) (src:1342)
GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44C(1) this section applies to the year` MEANS
    IF year's `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 2010
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says to which years the section applies

-- (3): a pensioner is eligible for earnings factor enhancement in respect of a week if one or more apply: (a) a relevant
-- carer for s 23A (seam S14); (b) carer's allowance payable for any part of the week, or would have been but for a
-- reduction to nil; (c) severe disablement allowance payable for any part of the week; (d) long-term incapacity benefit
-- payable for any part of the week or would have been but for (i) failing the contribution conditions or (ii) a
-- reduction to nil because of other benefits or scheme payments (schemes: subsection (4)); (e) another prescribed condition.
-- src:1348 | (3) A pensioner is eligible for earnings factor enhancement in respect of a week if one or more of the following apply—
-- src:1349 | (a) he was a relevant carer in respect of that week for the purposes of section 23A above (see section 23A(3));
-- src:1350 | (b) carer's allowance was payable to him for any part of that week, or would have been so payable but for the fact that under regulations the amount payable to him was reduced to nil because of his receipt of other benefits;
-- src:1351 | (c) severe disablement allowance was payable to him for any part of that week;
-- src:1352 | (d) long-term incapacity benefit was payable to him for any part of that week or would have been so payable but for the fact that—
-- src:1353 | (i) he did not satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3, or
-- src:1354 | (ii) under regulations the amount payable to him was reduced to nil because of his receipt of other benefits or of payments from an occupational pension scheme or personal pension scheme;
-- src:1355 | (e) he satisfies such other conditions as may be prescribed.
@ref s 44C(3) (src:1348-1355)
GIVEN `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `carer's allowance was payable for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `carer's allowance would have been so payable but for a reduction to nil under regulations because of the receipt of other benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `severe disablement allowance was payable for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `long-term incapacity benefit was payable for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner did not satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under regulations the amount payable was reduced to nil because of the receipt of other benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under regulations the amount payable was reduced to nil because of the receipt of payments from a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 30DD(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30DD(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner satisfies another condition prescribed for the purposes of paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44C(3) the pensioner is eligible for earnings factor enhancement in respect of the week` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A pensioner is eligible for earnings factor enhancement in respect of a week if one or more of the following apply" -- a failed "if" counts as the text's no (marginal reading (a))
    `ssc3 helper any of`
        (LIST
            `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week`
          , JUST `carer's allowance was payable for any part of the week`
          , JUST `carer's allowance would have been so payable but for a reduction to nil under regulations because of the receipt of other benefits`
          , JUST `severe disablement allowance was payable for any part of the week`
          , `ssc3 helper any of`
                (LIST
                    JUST `long-term incapacity benefit was payable for any part of the week`
                  , JUST `the pensioner did not satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3`
                  , JUST `under regulations the amount payable was reduced to nil because of the receipt of other benefits`
                  , `ssc3 helper all of`
                        (LIST
                            JUST `under regulations the amount payable was reduced to nil because of the receipt of payments from a scheme`
                          , `ssc3 helper any of` (LIST `s 30DD(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme`, `s 30DD(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme`)))
          , JUST `the pensioner satisfies another condition prescribed for the purposes of paragraph (e)`)

-- (2): for each week falling in a relevant year to which the section applies, in respect of which the pensioner is
-- eligible, the pensioner is entitled to a credit equal to 1/52 of the QEF for that year. ("This is subject to
-- subsection (5)": the cap, below.)
-- src:1343 | (2) In respect of each week—
-- src:1344 | (a) which falls in a relevant year to which this section applies, and
-- src:1345 | (b) in respect of which a pensioner is eligible for earnings factor enhancement,
-- src:1346 | the pensioner is entitled to an earnings factor credit equal to 1/52 of the QEF for that year.
-- src:1347 | This is subject to subsection (5) below.
@ref s 44C(2) (src:1343-1347)
GIVEN `the week falls in a relevant year to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner is eligible for earnings factor enhancement in respect of the week` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 44C(2) the earnings factor credit for the week in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the week falls in a relevant year to which this section applies` AND `the pensioner is eligible for earnings factor enhancement in respect of the week` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`the qualifying earnings factor for the year` DIVIDED BY 52)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the pensioner "is entitled to" a credit for a week that falls in a relevant year to which the section applies and in which the pensioner is eligible; the text does not say the pensioner is not entitled otherwise

-- (5): for Condition B a person is not entitled to an aggregate amount of credits for a year greater than the
-- difference referred to in that Condition (the QEF less the earnings factor apart from this section and s 44C).
-- src:1357 | (5) For the purposes of Condition B in section 44B(4) above a person is not entitled to an aggregate amount of earnings factor credits in respect of a year that is greater than the difference referred to in that Condition.
@ref s 44C(5) (src:1357)
GIVEN `the sum of the credits for the weeks of the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section and section 44C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 44C(5) the aggregate amount of credits the pensioner is entitled to for Condition B` MEANS
    min `the sum of the credits for the weeks of the year` (`the qualifying earnings factor for the year` MINUS `the pensioner's earnings factor for the year apart from this section and section 44C`)

-- (6): a week that falls partly in one tax year and partly in another is treated as falling in the year in which it
-- begins. The answer is the year, named by the calendar year in which it begins (6 April).
-- src:1358 | (6) For the purposes of this section a week that falls partly in one tax year and partly in another is to be treated as falling in the year in which it begins and not in the following year.
@ref s 44C(6) (src:1358)
GIVEN `the day on which the week begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 44C(6) the tax year the week is treated as falling in` MEANS
    `Tax year` OF (`ssc3 helper tax year of` `the day on which the week begins`)

-- (4): "occupational pension scheme" and "personal pension scheme" have the meanings given by s 30DD(6) for s 30DD(5).
-- src:1356 | (4) In subsection (3)(d)(ii) above “occupational pension scheme” and “personal pension scheme” have the meanings given by subsection (6) of section 30DD above for the purposes of subsection (5) of that section.
@ref s 44C(4) (src:1356)
GIVEN `s 30DD(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44C(4) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` MEANS `s 30DD(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme`

-- src:1356 | (4) In subsection (3)(d)(ii) above “occupational pension scheme” and “personal pension scheme” have the meanings given by subsection (6) of section 30DD above for the purposes of subsection (5) of that section.
@ref s 44C(4) (src:1356)
GIVEN `s 30DD(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44C(4) the scheme is a personal pension scheme` MEANS `s 30DD(6) the scheme is a personal pension scheme`

-- (7)(a): "the QEF" means the qualifying earnings factor (an input: it is set outside this Act's sources).
-- (7)(b): a reference to a person being entitled to an earnings factor credit of an amount (or an aggregate amount of
-- credits) for a year is a reference to the person being treated as having for that year an earnings factor
-- (within the meaning of s 44(6)(za)) of that amount.
-- src:1359 | (7) In section 44B above and this section—
-- src:1360 | (a) “the QEF” means the qualifying earnings factor, and
-- src:1361 | (b) any reference to a person being entitled to an earnings factor credit of a particular amount (or to an aggregate amount of earnings factor credits) for a year is a reference to the person being treated as having for that year an earnings factor (within the meaning of section 44(6)(za) above) of the amount in question by virtue of subsection (2) above.
@ref s 44C(7) (src:1359-1361)
GIVEN `the amount of earnings factor credit, or the aggregate amount of credits, the person is entitled to for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 44C(7)(b) the earnings factor the person is treated as having for the year by virtue of subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the amount of earnings factor credit, or the aggregate amount of credits, the person is entitled to for the year`
